# apps/web — example environment. Copy to .env.local; NEVER commit a filled-in
# copy (.env / .env.local are gitignored). The FULL variable list, with what
# each one does, is in AGENTS.md ("Frontend environment"); this file carries
# the Clerk pair, because those are the two people most often put in the wrong
# place. See docs/ARCHITECTURE.md §10.2 for why the auth switch is atomic.

# Clerk's publishable key — safe in the browser BY DESIGN (it is baked into the
# client bundle), but it still belongs in env and not in the tree, so staging
# and production instances cannot be swapped by a code edit. Unset it and the
# frontend mounts no provider at all and stays on the asserted dev identity,
# which is the rollback for the frontend half of the switch.
# Only read in apps/web/lib/mode.ts (isClerkEnabled) and by Clerk's own SDK.
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx

# CLERK_SECRET_KEY is deliberately NOT set here. This app verifies no token:
# it mounts Clerk in the browser and sends the JWT to the exam service, which
# is the only thing that checks it. The secret key belongs to that service
# (Cloud Run, mounted from Secret Manager by .github/workflows/deploy.yml).
# Add it here only if a server-rendered page in THIS repo ever calls auth().
# CLERK_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_xxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx
